 "split": "test",
 "source_instruction": "i would like a 7 by 5 foot long photo backdrop that is light weight and easy to carry.",
 "query": "Hey, I was out on my morning walk along the coastal trail earlier today and stopped to watch a group of teen skaters pull tricks off the weathered concrete ledge by the old lifeguard stand, right? One of them nailed a kickflip over a stray seagull that waddled right into their path at the last second, and the whole crowd that\u2019d gathered to watch cheered so loud a flock of pelicans took off from the nearby jetty. I stuck around for a few minutes to chat with them, and they told me they\u2019re raising money to fix up the cracked sections of the skate spot that\u2019ve been messed up since last winter\u2019s big storm knocked a bunch of driftwood onto it. It was such a nice, random little moment that it almost made me forget I burned my toast so bad this morning the smoke alarm went off and my cat hid under the couch for 20 minutes.\nAnyway, I\u2019m browsing the underwater photography section right now looking for gear for digital photography that\u2019s super light weight, yeah? Since you guys never seem to carry the light weight options I actually like, I\u2019ll just grab whatever similar lighter alternative you have handy instead. Can you point me to that one size I always get for these backdrops, yeah? I don\u2019t wanna spend too much, so just show me whatever fits what I\u2019m asking for without going over, like, a reasonable amount for this kind of thing, thanks.",
